  "rationale": "Resubmission of the round-3 accepted stream, which is optimal on both objectives. A's two 16x16 tiles (offsets 0 and 16, slot-0 stride 32 bytes) are loaded once into spad rows 0 and 16 and reused across all 5 column blocks \u2014 minimal A traffic of 512 bytes, since A is 16x32 = 512 int8 bytes and every element is used. Per block i = 0..N//16-1: mvin B(k=0..15) tile at offset 16*i into spad 32 (slot-1 stride 80), preload with overwrite out_addr 2684354560 (bit31|bit29, acc row 0), compute A tile 0 with accumulated=false and bd=4294967295; mvin B(k=16..31) tile at offset 1280 + 16*i (16*80 + 16*i, the true start of B rows 16..31 in the 32x80 row-major layout) into spad 48, preload with accumulate out_addr 3758096384 (bit31|bit30|bit29), compute A tile at spad 16 with accumulated=false; then mvout acc rows 0..15 (acc_addr 2684354560) to C element offset 16*i with store stride 320 (80 int32). Reduction order is k=0..15 then k=16..31, increasing K-index per cell, and K*16384 = 524288 <= 2147483647. Total mvin bytes: 2*256 (A) + 10*256 (B) = 3072, minimal since B is 32x80 = 2560 int8 bytes with all 10 distinct tiles loaded exactly once. Scratchpad: tiles at rows 0, 16, 32, 48 (48+16 = 64 <= 80), all 16-aligned; accumulator rows 0..15 within 16. Expanded commands: 6 setup + 7*5 loop + 1 fence = 42, minimal given 12 mandatory mvins, 10 computes each requiring its own preload, 5 mvouts, 4 configs, and a final fence."
